---- wgmma_config_sweep: WAVE 3's per-shape dispatcher (ptx_wgmma::wgmma_dispatch) ----
  A PURE function of (M, N, K, sm_count), device-free and unit-tested without a GPU:
  tile    the WIDEST of [128x256 s4, 128x128 s6, 128x64 s4] whose wave efficiency clears 0.90
  raster  iff the grid is multi-wave AND the LINEAR wave footprint blows L2 (52.4 MB)
  persist iff the grid is multi-wave
  cluster iff what a 1x2x1 B multicast would SAVE off the FINAL configuration's binding roof,
          f_L2 x (bn/2)/(bm+bn), clears 0.26 -- which is the 0.78 of WAVE3_DOSSIER 3.2 times the
          0.333 share it was fitted at (128x256). The share is 1/4 at 128x128 and 1/6 at 128x64, so a
          narrow tile is NOT judged by the wide tile's bar: sq1024 clears 0.78 on f_L2 and is still OFF.
  The raster enters the cluster decision through the FINAL footprint: it is what decides whether the
  memory roof is max(T_L2, T_DRAM) (L2-resident) or T_hit + T_DRAM (thrashing), which is why gpt_d4096_up's
  verdict differs between the two arms printed for it below. f_L2 here is T_L2 / T_PREDICTED, not 3.2's
  T_L2 / T_measured; the two differ by 0.4's residual and the bracket carries across (see
  CLUSTER_F_L2_THRESHOLD). It DECLINES rather than falling back: a fallback is how a round publishes a
  configuration that never ran.
  Each verdict below is measured by the row named beside it, at this shape, with its own control
  (the_dispatcher_verdict_is_pinned_at_every_benched_shape and every_shape_the_dispatcher_selects_is_measured_at_that_shape
  are the device-free laws).
